1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,770
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,770 --> 00:00:03,540
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,540 --> 00:00:05,310
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:07,810
(Episode 47)

5
00:00:16,390 --> 00:00:19,020
You must've been so lonely
all these years.

6
00:00:19,590 --> 00:00:22,890
I want to ease
that emotional burden of yours, sir.

7
00:00:24,330 --> 00:00:25,560
No matter what happens,

8
00:00:26,330 --> 00:00:28,470
I will always be on your side.

9
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:07,310
When the time comes,
I'll tell you everything.

10
00:01:08,610 --> 00:01:09,710
I feel like...

11
00:01:10,680 --> 00:01:12,210
I can confide in you.

12
00:01:14,380 --> 00:01:15,380
Okay.

13
00:01:16,180 --> 00:01:17,220
I'll wait.

14
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:37,900
Eun Guk.

15
00:01:38,440 --> 00:01:39,940
Ko Eun Guk.

16
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:45,380
Darn it.

17
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:48,480
Did that punk sneak off again
the second he opened his eyes?

18
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:52,850
Maybe I ought to break his legs
to keep him put.

19
00:01:54,250 --> 00:01:55,320
Wait.

20
00:01:57,190 --> 00:01:58,590
Instead of just standing around,

21
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:01,760
shouldn't I stick close
and keep an eye on him?

22
00:02:04,130 --> 00:02:05,630
We're not open yet.

23
00:02:07,630 --> 00:02:08,630
Grandma.

24
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:10,840
Morning.

25
00:02:11,770 --> 00:02:14,340
You seem awfully busy
for a place with no customers.

26
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:15,910
We're about to open.

27
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:18,010
What brings you here, Grandma?

28
00:02:18,410 --> 00:02:19,640
Why else?

29
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:22,850
I just swung by to see
if I could lend a hand.

30
00:02:22,910 --> 00:02:23,950
You?

31
00:02:24,650 --> 00:02:27,120
Your mind must still be
all over the place.

32
00:02:27,650 --> 00:02:29,750
Having me around
making a bit of noise...

33
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:31,560
might take your mind off things
for a bit.

34
00:02:32,420 --> 00:02:33,890
That really isn't necessary.

35
00:02:36,390 --> 00:02:37,430
Be honest.

36
00:02:37,630 --> 00:02:38,730
You came to keep tabs on me.

37
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:40,060
As if.

38
00:02:40,130 --> 00:02:41,830
I told you,
I'm here to help Teun Teun's Mom.

39
00:02:43,030 --> 00:02:44,970
Eun Guk, can you take this outside?

40
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:46,040
Sure.

41
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:47,240
No, leave it.

42
00:02:47,970 --> 00:02:49,010
Let me.

43
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:50,480
Gosh, that's heavy.

44
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:53,850
Why is this so heavy?

45
00:03:00,020 --> 00:03:02,350
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

46
00:03:02,920 --> 00:03:04,160
Did you get home all right
yesterday?

47
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:05,720
Yes.

48
00:03:06,590 --> 00:03:08,230
My mom was very worried about you.

49
00:03:09,190 --> 00:03:10,760
You should've just let me
drive you home.

50
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:14,630
Sorry about that.
I reached out to her separately.

51
00:03:16,130 --> 00:03:17,840
All right, thanks.

52
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:19,140
Then...

53
00:03:19,940 --> 00:03:20,940
Ko Eun Seol.

54
00:03:24,510 --> 00:03:27,550
Seeing you yesterday,
you looked comfortable around her.

55
00:03:29,850 --> 00:03:31,620
If being with her
brings you comfort,

56
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:34,450
feel free to see her,
regardless of how I feel.

57
00:03:34,690 --> 00:03:36,620
Would that really be okay?

58
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:39,260
Hae Ra might feel
pretty uncomfortable with that.

59
00:03:39,990 --> 00:03:42,160
I'll explain things to her,
so don't worry about that.

60
00:03:45,730 --> 00:03:47,430
Thank you for understanding.

61
00:03:58,710 --> 00:04:00,040
The last time
I went to So Yeon's house,

62
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:01,380
we talked about the accident,

63
00:04:02,110 --> 00:04:03,880
and I heard Oh Tae Seop's name.

64
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:06,990
According to So Yeon,

65
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:09,320
a man named Oh Tae Seop...

66
00:04:09,390 --> 00:04:12,160
was behind the accident
involving Chief Cha's father.

67
00:04:16,090 --> 00:04:17,360
Hey, you're here.

68
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:19,360
Have a seat.

69
00:04:21,530 --> 00:04:23,430
It's not like you
to call me in at this hour, Dad.

70
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:24,940
What's this about?

71
00:04:25,340 --> 00:04:26,740
It's nothing serious.

72
00:04:27,370 --> 00:04:29,610
Just about you and Chief Cha.

73
00:04:30,140 --> 00:04:31,840
About our engagement?

74
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:33,140
That, too.

75
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:36,110
Based on what you've seen,

76
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:38,520
how does So Yeon seem?

77
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:41,250
Ms. Park's the same as always.

78
00:04:41,950 --> 00:04:44,460
She doesn't even seem to have
the mind of an elementary schooler.

79
00:04:46,090 --> 00:04:49,360
What does Chief Cha say
he'll do with her?

80
00:04:49,630 --> 00:04:52,200
Does he plan on living with her
even after marriage?

81
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:53,770
Of course.

82
00:04:53,830 --> 00:04:55,730
Seok Jin worships the ground
she walks on.

83
00:04:56,770 --> 00:05:00,340
I feel like I'll spend my whole life
waiting on Ms. Park.

84
00:05:01,410 --> 00:05:02,510
With a mother-in-law like her,

85
00:05:02,510 --> 00:05:04,210
it'd be better to have
no in-laws at all.

86
00:05:04,310 --> 00:05:05,810
Poor me, right?

87
00:05:07,710 --> 00:05:11,720
How about you casually
bring it up with Chief Cha?

88
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:14,620
Ask him how he feels about
putting her somewhere with fresh air.

89
00:05:15,090 --> 00:05:16,790
If I do that, he'll flip out again.

90
00:05:17,220 --> 00:05:19,260
When he overheard the Director
and me talking about it,

91
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:20,960
he threw such a massive fit.

92
00:05:21,260 --> 00:05:23,490
That's why you need
to be tactful about it.

93
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:26,230
Now isn't the right time,

94
00:05:26,630 --> 00:05:30,800
so wait until after you're engaged
to bring it up again naturally.

95
00:05:31,100 --> 00:05:32,500
I'll give you a hand.

96
00:05:32,770 --> 00:05:34,770
Really? You'll help me, Dad?

97
00:05:35,640 --> 00:05:38,880
You don't want your daughter
suffering under a mother-in-law.

98
00:05:39,940 --> 00:05:43,080
Of course not.
You're my precious daughter.

99
00:05:44,050 --> 00:05:45,050
All right.

100
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:47,090
I'll casually mention it
to him again later.

101
00:05:48,950 --> 00:05:49,950
Good.

102
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:01,400
Secretary Choi.

103
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:04,500
There's something I want to ask.

104
00:06:05,370 --> 00:06:07,070
Sure, what is it?

105
00:06:08,340 --> 00:06:12,610
In your eyes,
what kind of person is Director Joo?

106
00:06:13,810 --> 00:06:14,880
The Director?

107
00:06:15,150 --> 00:06:16,150
Yes.

108
00:06:17,450 --> 00:06:21,650
She's meticulous about everything
and is a total workaholic.

109
00:06:22,250 --> 00:06:25,120
From the scholarship foundation
to Cheongma Group's PR,

110
00:06:25,220 --> 00:06:26,620
she oversees it all.

111
00:06:27,830 --> 00:06:30,030
She's close
to the CEO as well, right?

112
00:06:30,190 --> 00:06:31,200
Yes.

113
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:34,900
Though if I had to say,
she's closer to the Chairman.

114
00:06:37,140 --> 00:06:38,140
But...

115
00:06:38,670 --> 00:06:40,140
why are you suddenly curious
about that?

116
00:06:42,810 --> 00:06:45,540
She has been helping out a lot
with our scholarship program.

117
00:06:46,140 --> 00:06:47,850
I was just wondering
what kind of person she is.

118
00:06:49,580 --> 00:06:50,580
I see.

119
00:06:59,060 --> 00:07:01,160
Did you look into places
to put An Guk Cheol?

120
00:07:01,230 --> 00:07:03,960
Yes, I looked into a few places
out of town,

121
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:07,030
but the admission process
is trickier than expected.

122
00:07:08,230 --> 00:07:10,300
Once we get someone
to manage the paperwork,

123
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:11,640
I'll get the ball rolling.

124
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:14,310
So that's that for An Guk Cheol.

125
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:16,570
How has Ko Eun Seol been doing?

126
00:07:17,580 --> 00:07:18,580
Lately...

127
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:22,280
She seems to be
focusing more on work.

128
00:07:22,850 --> 00:07:26,780
I haven't really noticed her doing
anything out of the ordinary.

129
00:07:27,150 --> 00:07:28,890
Keep a close eye on her
at all times.

130
00:07:29,290 --> 00:07:31,220
If she's digging into my past...

131
00:07:31,290 --> 00:07:33,060
or you feel like she's prying,

132
00:07:33,060 --> 00:07:34,260
report it instantly.

133
00:07:36,090 --> 00:07:38,030
Yes, will do.

134
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:12,030
What is this, a 60th birthday party?

135
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:14,400
The whole setup looks
drab and tacky.

136
00:08:15,130 --> 00:08:17,900
Find another florist,
and rebook the venue too.

137
00:08:18,570 --> 00:08:20,200
- You're dismissed.
- Yes, Ms. Kang.

138
00:08:24,910 --> 00:08:25,940
Ms. Ko.

139
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:28,450
You didn't forget
our ring tour tomorrow, right?

140
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:29,680
I didn't.

141
00:08:30,410 --> 00:08:32,080
Go on ahead and pull a few options.

142
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:34,650
Seok Jin and I will meet you there
right after our suit fitting.

143
00:08:41,830 --> 00:08:44,100
Grandma, head home already.

144
00:08:44,860 --> 00:08:47,230
You must be exhausted
after doing all the work for me.

145
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:48,500
I'm about to collapse.

146
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:52,140
How can such a small place
require so much work?

147
00:08:53,470 --> 00:08:56,640
I'll keep my distance
from your grandson while closing up,

148
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:57,740
so please head home.

149
00:08:58,480 --> 00:09:00,650
Fine. Whether you two
stick together...

150
00:09:01,110 --> 00:09:04,280
and make eyes at each other
or whatever,

151
00:09:04,350 --> 00:09:05,350
I couldn't care less.

152
00:09:05,580 --> 00:09:07,320
My arms, legs, and back...

153
00:09:09,820 --> 00:09:11,390
This is killing me.

154
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:18,830
Mom, where are you going?

155
00:09:18,830 --> 00:09:20,560
Don't ask, you punk.

156
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:23,400
Hey.

157
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:25,540
Has your grandma been here
this whole time?

158
00:09:25,770 --> 00:09:27,170
To keep an eye on me, yes.

159
00:09:27,370 --> 00:09:30,340
Man, talk about total devotion.

160
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:32,080
Mom,

161
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:34,780
can you buy me some battle cards?

162
00:09:35,050 --> 00:09:36,080
Right now?

163
00:09:36,780 --> 00:09:38,380
But I have to close up the shop.

164
00:09:39,650 --> 00:09:41,590
Teun Teun, I'll take you.

165
00:09:42,450 --> 00:09:43,520
Really?

166
00:09:45,560 --> 00:09:46,920
Right, go ahead.

167
00:09:47,690 --> 00:09:48,930
Now, what else?

168
00:09:50,090 --> 00:09:51,160
It's okay. I'll get that.

169
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:52,430
When it comes to cleaning,

170
00:09:52,660 --> 00:09:55,330
I bet I'm much better at it
than you.

171
00:09:56,670 --> 00:09:57,700
Thank you.

172
00:09:58,470 --> 00:10:00,170
Why would you thank me every day?

173
00:10:00,710 --> 00:10:02,770
We're all family here.

174
00:10:03,570 --> 00:10:06,740
You know, when you're troubled,

175
00:10:06,810 --> 00:10:11,180
being around others
makes things so much better.

176
00:10:11,650 --> 00:10:13,780
Don't think you have
to raise Teun Teun all on your own.

177
00:10:13,950 --> 00:10:16,550
Why do everything yourself
when you have such a big family?

178
00:10:19,460 --> 00:10:21,630
Still, your mother must be worried.

179
00:10:21,790 --> 00:10:25,060
She's already been stressing so much
over Eun Guk and me.

180
00:10:25,530 --> 00:10:28,300
My mom might look really tough
on the outside,

181
00:10:28,730 --> 00:10:31,800
but she's actually
the softest person in the world.

182
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,940
What do they call it,
a tough softie?

183
00:10:34,210 --> 00:10:35,940
She acts prickly,

184
00:10:36,010 --> 00:10:37,440
but deep down,
she has a very tender heart.

185
00:10:37,580 --> 00:10:38,980
Don't mind my mom,

186
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:40,080
and just focus on...

187
00:10:40,410 --> 00:10:44,480
getting your peace of mind
back for now, okay?

188
00:10:47,150 --> 00:10:50,050
All right.
Wait, what did I come here to do?

189
00:10:50,820 --> 00:10:53,460
I guess cleaning really is
second nature to me.

190
00:10:54,530 --> 00:10:57,130
They're going
ring shopping tomorrow?

191
00:10:57,560 --> 00:10:58,630
Yes.

192
00:10:58,700 --> 00:11:02,270
They want to get custom-made ones,
so they're getting a head start.

193
00:11:02,730 --> 00:11:05,800
Oh, and about So Yeon...

194
00:11:07,670 --> 00:11:10,270
I was thinking,
with a little help from us,

195
00:11:10,340 --> 00:11:12,710
maybe she can go back
to how she used to be.

196
00:11:14,550 --> 00:11:16,550
What do you mean by that?

197
00:11:16,750 --> 00:11:19,750
I mean So Yeon's memories,
from before the accident.

198
00:11:22,090 --> 00:11:26,290
I feel like regular therapy
for her trauma...

199
00:11:26,460 --> 00:11:28,830
could make a real difference.

200
00:11:32,100 --> 00:11:33,960
Can we really just stand by
and do nothing?

201
00:11:36,070 --> 00:11:37,370
- Honey?
- Darn it.

202
00:11:37,670 --> 00:11:39,400
- Are you okay?
- There must be ointment somewhere.

203
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:42,010
Wait. It's in Hae Ra's room.
I know where it is.

204
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:45,110
Here.

205
00:11:45,180 --> 00:11:49,280
Hold this for now.
It'll feel much better.

206
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:57,920
Thank you, Director Joo.

207
00:12:02,830 --> 00:12:05,730
Honey, are you okay?

208
00:12:08,130 --> 00:12:10,270
- Apply some of this.
- Give it here.

209
00:12:10,270 --> 00:12:13,100
- It's swollen already.
- Just give it here.

210
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:14,910
I'll do it myself.

211
00:12:22,580 --> 00:12:24,750
Look at how swollen it is already.

212
00:12:37,630 --> 00:12:40,500
I mean So Yeon's memories,
from before the accident.

213
00:12:59,450 --> 00:13:01,190
(Cheongma)

214
00:13:08,660 --> 00:13:10,230
Doesn't my husband...

215
00:13:10,830 --> 00:13:12,930
seem a little off lately?

216
00:13:14,270 --> 00:13:15,270
Pardon?

217
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:17,770
He seems so on edge.

218
00:13:19,070 --> 00:13:21,940
I need to know what's going on
to help him.

219
00:13:24,780 --> 00:13:26,840
Do you know anything, Director Joo?

220
00:13:28,350 --> 00:13:29,510
Well,

221
00:13:29,580 --> 00:13:31,920
with his workload
in the food division increasing,

222
00:13:31,980 --> 00:13:34,450
it's clear the stress is getting
to him.

223
00:13:35,350 --> 00:13:36,550
Even when things get tough,

224
00:13:36,590 --> 00:13:39,020
the CEO hardly ever opens up,
as you know.

225
00:13:40,260 --> 00:13:43,330
True. He isn't a man of many words.

226
00:13:44,330 --> 00:13:48,130
Still, between husband and wife,
there shouldn't be any secrets.

227
00:13:50,070 --> 00:13:51,840
If something truly difficult
comes up,

228
00:13:51,900 --> 00:13:54,670
he will tell you first, ma'am.

229
00:13:58,440 --> 00:14:01,980
I used to like his steadfastness,

230
00:14:03,450 --> 00:14:06,780
but lately,
it's just so frustrating.

231
00:14:08,690 --> 00:14:10,390
Don't worry too much.

232
00:14:11,090 --> 00:14:12,520
I'm sure it's nothing.

233
00:14:13,560 --> 00:14:14,790
I suppose.

234
00:14:15,090 --> 00:14:17,030
He's never acted like this before,

235
00:14:17,090 --> 00:14:18,500
so I can't help feeling worried.

236
00:14:30,110 --> 00:14:31,610
I'm on my way.

237
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:33,180
Well, hurry.

238
00:14:33,210 --> 00:14:35,150
We're all finished with the fitting
and on our way now.

239
00:14:35,410 --> 00:14:37,050
It'll take about 30 minutes.

240
00:14:37,620 --> 00:14:39,350
You know my ring size
and his, right?

241
00:14:40,350 --> 00:14:41,350
Yes.

242
00:14:56,970 --> 00:14:58,840
I came here to ask you something.

243
00:15:04,980 --> 00:15:07,880
My dad said
if anything ever happened to him,

244
00:15:08,510 --> 00:15:10,280
I need to make sure this gets shown.

245
00:15:12,720 --> 00:15:15,720
And Attorney Seo took it?

246
00:15:16,220 --> 00:15:17,220
Yes.

247
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:20,160
The police said
it was completely useless,

248
00:15:20,220 --> 00:15:21,630
so I gave it to him.

249
00:15:22,530 --> 00:15:24,530
He said he would help me.

250
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:29,230
Do you know what it was?

251
00:15:31,300 --> 00:15:32,370
It was...

252
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:35,210
a picture of my dad with someone.

253
00:15:36,740 --> 00:15:38,610
There was some kind
of bracelet, too.

254
00:15:40,110 --> 00:15:41,110
A bracelet?

255
00:15:43,310 --> 00:15:45,580
And there was the fountain pen
my dad always cherished.

256
00:15:51,020 --> 00:15:52,720
I was so shocked by the news.

257
00:15:54,090 --> 00:15:55,160
Attorney Seo...

258
00:15:56,030 --> 00:15:59,030
He said he'd help both you and me.

259
00:16:00,200 --> 00:16:01,200
But...

260
00:16:02,230 --> 00:16:05,440
I never imagined something like that
would happen to him.

261
00:16:09,210 --> 00:16:10,870
He didn't die because of me, right?

262
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:14,110
What if he died trying to help me?

263
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:20,420
I'm sure that's not it.

264
00:16:21,450 --> 00:16:23,720
First, I'll look for those items.

265
00:16:24,490 --> 00:16:25,490
Mom.

266
00:16:25,820 --> 00:16:27,730
- You're home, Seok Jin?
- Hey.

267
00:16:28,930 --> 00:16:31,130
Right. Hi, Hae Ra.

268
00:16:31,500 --> 00:16:34,230
Hello, Mother. Here you go.

269
00:16:34,470 --> 00:16:38,040
I brought you some cake to try.
People line up for this place.

270
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:40,400
Thanks.

271
00:16:44,210 --> 00:16:45,410
Where are you going, Mom?

272
00:16:46,140 --> 00:16:47,440
Let's eat it together here.

273
00:16:49,480 --> 00:16:52,020
No, it's fine. You two go ahead.

274
00:17:05,700 --> 00:17:07,770
Did Ko Eun Seol
really just bolt on us?

275
00:17:08,170 --> 00:17:11,140
She thinks she can ignore plans
with her supervisor?

276
00:17:11,470 --> 00:17:12,770
She's dead tomorrow.

277
00:17:13,140 --> 00:17:15,270
As if. You were being unreasonable.

278
00:17:16,010 --> 00:17:19,710
No employee should ever have to go
ring shopping with their boss.

279
00:17:19,980 --> 00:17:22,180
Whatever.
I'm just annoyed by everything.

280
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:28,050
Seok Jin, should I stay the night?

281
00:17:28,250 --> 00:17:29,320
Forget it.

282
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:31,790
Say goodbye to my mom.
I'll drive you home.

283
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:34,160
You're really making me leave?

284
00:17:34,430 --> 00:17:35,990
Do you want to sleep
in my mom's room, then?

285
00:17:39,300 --> 00:17:40,430
Come on, hurry up.

286
00:17:43,130 --> 00:17:45,570
The police said
it was completely useless,

287
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:47,040
so I gave it to him.

288
00:17:47,940 --> 00:17:50,010
He said he would help me.

289
00:17:50,410 --> 00:17:52,280
He didn't die because of me, right?

290
00:17:52,840 --> 00:17:55,450
What if he died trying to help me?

291
00:17:57,950 --> 00:18:02,850
Does this mean Manager Na knew
something bad would happen to him?

292
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:12,260
What message was he trying to send
with those items?

293
00:18:18,300 --> 00:18:19,300
Mom, are you asleep?

294
00:18:19,870 --> 00:18:24,210
Not yet.
I'm about to go to sleep, though.

295
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:30,550
Mom, are you still uncomfortable
around Hae Ra?

296
00:18:30,850 --> 00:18:32,150
Not at all.

297
00:18:32,880 --> 00:18:36,350
Hae Ra said
she would make you happy, Seok Jin.

298
00:18:37,490 --> 00:18:41,930
So from now on,
I'm going to try to like her.

299
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:45,360
Then why do you always avoid her?

300
00:18:46,730 --> 00:18:49,800
Are you scared of her
or intimidated by her?

301
00:18:49,900 --> 00:18:52,370
No, she doesn't scare me.

302
00:18:54,300 --> 00:18:57,570
There is someone else
who is truly terrifying.

303
00:18:58,380 --> 00:18:59,380
Who?

304
00:19:00,010 --> 00:19:01,180
Young Hoon.

305
00:19:02,180 --> 00:19:04,480
Young Hoon? You mean CEO Kang?

306
00:19:04,820 --> 00:19:08,020
Young Hoon's terrifying
when he gets mad.

307
00:19:08,290 --> 00:19:09,720
He screams...

308
00:19:10,550 --> 00:19:11,620
and curses.

309
00:19:12,560 --> 00:19:13,890
How do you know that, Mom?

310
00:19:14,060 --> 00:19:15,390
I just do.

311
00:19:16,460 --> 00:19:19,200
He got so angry at my darling.

312
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,470
It was so scary.

313
00:19:22,930 --> 00:19:23,970
Right?

314
00:19:26,840 --> 00:19:28,070
I should go to bed.

315
00:19:31,580 --> 00:19:32,580
There.

316
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:34,110
(Cheongma)

317
00:19:40,620 --> 00:19:41,720
What happened to you yesterday?

318
00:19:42,090 --> 00:19:43,090
I'm sorry.

319
00:19:43,320 --> 00:19:44,760
As if you really are.

320
00:19:45,220 --> 00:19:47,320
Is your superior a joke to you?

321
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:49,360
You think one text
makes it all okay?

322
00:19:49,430 --> 00:19:51,700
Do you know how stunned
Seok Jin and I were yesterday?

323
00:19:51,960 --> 00:19:54,130
Something came up on my end,

324
00:19:54,130 --> 00:19:55,870
but didn't you get
your rings anyway?

325
00:19:57,100 --> 00:19:58,100
Sure.

326
00:19:58,440 --> 00:20:00,900
They had the design I wanted,
so it worked out.

327
00:20:01,240 --> 00:20:03,270
Still, it leaves a bad taste
in my mouth.

328
00:20:06,210 --> 00:20:07,910
If you didn't bail on purpose,

329
00:20:07,980 --> 00:20:09,780
show your sincerity
at the engagement party.

330
00:20:10,110 --> 00:20:12,250
- What?
- You will...

331
00:20:12,320 --> 00:20:14,220
come to our engagement party...

332
00:20:15,090 --> 00:20:17,150
and congratulate us
from the bottom of your heart.

333
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:25,600
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

334
00:20:26,430 --> 00:20:30,270
Young Hoon's terrifying
when he gets mad.

335
00:20:30,470 --> 00:20:32,940
He screams and curses.

336
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:40,640
This is Cha Seok Jin.

337
00:20:40,910 --> 00:20:43,180
Could you please check
the CEO's schedule for today?

338
00:20:44,380 --> 00:20:46,950
So, did you get
the rings you wanted?

339
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:49,590
Yes, we got them.

340
00:20:50,150 --> 00:20:52,920
Ko Eun Seol completely flaked on us,
which ruined my mood,

341
00:20:53,620 --> 00:20:56,760
but Seok Jin let me choose the style
I wanted this time.

342
00:20:57,130 --> 00:21:00,460
He won't be able to treat you
like he used to.

343
00:21:01,230 --> 00:21:04,470
Without you, he can't move up
a single step at Cheongma.

344
00:21:04,770 --> 00:21:05,770
You're right.

345
00:21:06,070 --> 00:21:08,310
No matter how talented Seok Jin is,

346
00:21:08,440 --> 00:21:11,340
how could his talent compare
to being my man?

347
00:21:12,010 --> 00:21:14,280
It seems he's slowly starting
to realize that too.

348
00:21:15,050 --> 00:21:18,680
That's why you need to solidify
your position even more.

349
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:21,690
That way,
Chief Cha will respect you...

350
00:21:21,690 --> 00:21:23,090
and won't look down on you.

351
00:21:24,150 --> 00:21:27,020
I want to do that too,
but Mom isn't helping at all.

352
00:21:27,390 --> 00:21:29,460
She won't even let me touch
the scholarship foundation work.

353
00:21:30,530 --> 00:21:32,930
I'll talk to the CEO
separately about it.

354
00:21:33,430 --> 00:21:35,630
You should also bring it up
to the Chairman again.

355
00:21:37,130 --> 00:21:38,600
You need to get your foot
in the door...

356
00:21:38,970 --> 00:21:41,170
at the scholarship foundation
by any means necessary.

357
00:21:43,170 --> 00:21:44,170
I will.

358
00:21:48,150 --> 00:21:50,210
You want to learn the ropes
at the scholarship foundation?

359
00:21:50,780 --> 00:21:52,820
Yes, it's like I said.

360
00:21:53,420 --> 00:21:55,590
If it's something
I'll have to take over eventually,

361
00:21:55,650 --> 00:21:57,550
shouldn't I start learning it now?

362
00:21:58,190 --> 00:21:59,820
I made myself pretty clear too.

363
00:22:00,220 --> 00:22:03,530
Once my scholarship program
gets reviewed positively,

364
00:22:03,530 --> 00:22:05,660
we can revisit the idea.

365
00:22:05,930 --> 00:22:07,200
It's still too early.

366
00:22:07,500 --> 00:22:09,230
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation,
Chairman Kim Jung Sun)

367
00:22:09,230 --> 00:22:11,370
Then just like Ko Eun Seol,
I'll help you out.

368
00:22:12,240 --> 00:22:13,570
With our scholarship program?

369
00:22:13,970 --> 00:22:16,810
Yes. Rather than launching something
under my own name right away,

370
00:22:16,940 --> 00:22:19,840
I could learn the ropes
by assisting with your program.

371
00:22:20,340 --> 00:22:21,910
No one can say anything
about that, right?

372
00:22:22,780 --> 00:22:24,080
Well, yes.

373
00:22:24,080 --> 00:22:26,880
Starting out that way
doesn't sound so bad.

374
00:22:28,050 --> 00:22:30,850
But can you really work
under Eun Seol?

375
00:22:30,990 --> 00:22:33,060
Putting your status
as her superior behind you?

376
00:22:33,820 --> 00:22:35,090
I guess I have no choice.

377
00:22:35,590 --> 00:22:37,560
As long as I can start working
at the foundation,

378
00:22:37,830 --> 00:22:39,900
I'll put up with it, even if
it's annoying and humiliating.

379
00:22:40,100 --> 00:22:42,400
Gosh, my daughter is all grown up.

380
00:22:43,030 --> 00:22:46,640
I had no idea you were this serious
about the foundation's work.

381
00:22:47,670 --> 00:22:48,670
All right, then.

382
00:22:48,740 --> 00:22:50,840
Start by attending
the meeting today.

383
00:22:51,780 --> 00:22:52,780
Okay.

384
00:22:54,280 --> 00:22:57,610
Hae Ra wants to help
with the foundation's work?

385
00:22:58,120 --> 00:23:01,420
Yes, she wants to learn
the scholarship business.

386
00:23:01,890 --> 00:23:05,120
Above all, Hae Ra needs
to succeed the Chairman.

387
00:23:06,120 --> 00:23:08,020
If she learns things sooner,

388
00:23:08,160 --> 00:23:10,160
she'll be able to speed up
that process.

389
00:23:10,730 --> 00:23:12,360
Well, that's true.

390
00:23:13,460 --> 00:23:17,500
My wife also seems to find
the Chairman role overwhelming.

391
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:19,940
I'll support Hae Ra closely...

392
00:23:20,300 --> 00:23:23,370
so she can solidify her position
at the scholarship foundation.

393
00:23:25,040 --> 00:23:27,740
Right. Director Joo,
help Hae Ra look into...

394
00:23:28,280 --> 00:23:30,610
a project for the foundation.

395
00:23:30,910 --> 00:23:32,480
I'll back her up.

396
00:23:33,880 --> 00:23:35,390
Yes, I'll do that.

397
00:23:36,590 --> 00:23:40,320
Having you around really
puts my mind at ease, Director Joo.

398
00:23:40,590 --> 00:23:43,690
Even with your busy schedule,
you look after Hae Ra as well.

399
00:23:44,060 --> 00:23:46,160
The future of Cheongma
depends on it.

400
00:23:46,730 --> 00:23:47,860
Indeed.

401
00:23:49,230 --> 00:23:50,230
Why is my wife...

402
00:23:50,870 --> 00:23:53,070
the only one blind
to that simple truth?

403
00:23:59,540 --> 00:24:00,540
Right.

404
00:24:10,550 --> 00:24:11,890
Thank you, Director Joo.

405
00:24:19,460 --> 00:24:22,570
First, let's open up applications
for the mentoring program.

406
00:24:23,030 --> 00:24:25,140
Sure, I'll gather
all the recommendations...

407
00:24:25,140 --> 00:24:26,140
from each institution.

408
00:24:32,110 --> 00:24:33,610
What are you staring at?

409
00:24:33,740 --> 00:24:36,410
What brings you here, Ms. Kang?

410
00:24:36,580 --> 00:24:38,750
Starting today, I'll be helping out
with the foundation work.

411
00:24:40,220 --> 00:24:41,850
- You, Ms. Kang?
- Yes.

412
00:24:42,320 --> 00:24:45,520
To take over my mom's work,
I need to learn ahead of time.

413
00:24:46,290 --> 00:24:49,030
I'll be attending meetings
from now on, so keep that in mind.

414
00:24:49,590 --> 00:24:52,130
Anything you need to report
goes through me first.

415
00:24:53,130 --> 00:24:55,100
I think you're mistaken
about something.

416
00:24:55,870 --> 00:24:56,900
Shouldn't you understand the work...

417
00:24:57,700 --> 00:24:59,200
before asking for reports?

418
00:25:00,940 --> 00:25:02,670
If you expect to be briefed,

419
00:25:05,540 --> 00:25:06,710
start with these documents
right here...

420
00:25:07,280 --> 00:25:08,550
and review them all.

421
00:25:10,480 --> 00:25:11,550
All of this?

422
00:25:11,950 --> 00:25:12,950
Yes.

423
00:25:13,180 --> 00:25:14,990
Yes, if the reporting line
is changing,

424
00:25:15,390 --> 00:25:17,090
then for the sake of the workflow,

425
00:25:17,320 --> 00:25:19,290
I hope you get up to speed quickly.

426
00:25:21,490 --> 00:25:23,290
Fine, when do I need to finish by?

427
00:25:23,460 --> 00:25:24,460
I'd appreciate it...

428
00:25:24,860 --> 00:25:26,200
if you could finish today.

429
00:25:38,040 --> 00:25:39,540
Why is this so complicated?

430
00:25:39,680 --> 00:25:41,010
There's just no end to it.

431
00:25:41,680 --> 00:25:43,210
How am I supposed to finish
all this today?

432
00:25:43,280 --> 00:25:44,480
Whatever, I quit.

433
00:25:49,320 --> 00:25:51,860
Director, please help me.

434
00:25:55,960 --> 00:25:56,960
What?

435
00:25:57,890 --> 00:25:59,260
What brings you here
at this time of day?

436
00:26:02,200 --> 00:26:04,700
I need to talk to Mi Rae.

437
00:26:07,440 --> 00:26:10,470
So you're saying Attorney Seo
had something in his possession?

438
00:26:11,410 --> 00:26:13,310
Yes, we need to find it...

439
00:26:13,380 --> 00:26:15,750
so we can discover
what he was trying to uncover.

440
00:26:17,210 --> 00:26:19,380
The police took most of his things,

441
00:26:19,780 --> 00:26:22,450
but some of his belongings
haven't been sorted out yet.

442
00:26:23,590 --> 00:26:25,520
Even if the police did find it,

443
00:26:25,720 --> 00:26:27,990
they likely wouldn't have seen it
as key evidence.

444
00:26:29,690 --> 00:26:31,260
Then let's go find it ourselves.

445
00:26:44,210 --> 00:26:45,210
Director,

446
00:26:45,880 --> 00:26:47,810
can't you fire your new secretary?

447
00:26:49,150 --> 00:26:50,880
- Secretary Choi?
- Yes.

448
00:26:52,080 --> 00:26:54,250
Didn't you recommend him yourself?

449
00:26:55,020 --> 00:26:57,390
I did, but...

450
00:26:58,120 --> 00:27:00,460
He shows absolute zero respect
for his superiors.

451
00:27:01,690 --> 00:27:03,760
How can you expect
to only hire people...

452
00:27:03,760 --> 00:27:05,030
who suit your personal taste?

453
00:27:05,630 --> 00:27:07,660
You also need employees
who speak the hard truth.

454
00:27:08,260 --> 00:27:09,470
Hard truth, my foot.

455
00:27:09,800 --> 00:27:11,670
Because of him,
even simple things get messed up.

456
00:27:12,740 --> 00:27:15,740
Managing people like that
is how you build leadership skills.

457
00:27:16,610 --> 00:27:19,010
Whatever, it's so frustrating.

458
00:27:20,240 --> 00:27:21,510
Just hang in there.

459
00:27:22,380 --> 00:27:25,280
Eventually,
all of Cheongma will be yours.

460
00:27:39,160 --> 00:27:41,330
(Cheongma Group's 50th Anniversary:
Announcing a Global Leap Forward)

461
00:27:41,400 --> 00:27:42,400
What?

462
00:27:43,070 --> 00:27:44,730
Am I supposed to just rot away
and die here?

463
00:27:45,800 --> 00:27:48,070
Why would I die at your hands?

464
00:27:51,410 --> 00:27:52,710
Just wait until I find my daughter.

465
00:27:53,240 --> 00:27:54,710
For everything you did to me,

466
00:27:55,410 --> 00:27:58,350
I'll make you pay back a hundredfold
in tears of blood.

467
00:28:00,980 --> 00:28:01,990
Joo Ae Sook.

468
00:28:03,290 --> 00:28:04,420
Just you wait.

469
00:28:34,250 --> 00:28:36,550
So this is where Ae Sook works?

470
00:28:37,290 --> 00:28:38,320
Unbelievable.

471
00:28:38,760 --> 00:28:39,760
Joo Ae Sook.

472
00:28:40,860 --> 00:28:42,690
You've really made it.

473
00:28:49,770 --> 00:28:50,970
What the heck?

474
00:28:50,970 --> 00:28:52,540
Gosh, I'm so sorry.

475
00:28:52,800 --> 00:28:55,370
What are you doing?
Are you kidding me?

476
00:28:55,370 --> 00:28:57,110
Why is nothing going my way today?

477
00:28:57,510 --> 00:28:59,040
I'm sorry. What should I do?

478
00:29:03,850 --> 00:29:04,950
What are you looking at?

479
00:29:06,080 --> 00:29:10,620
Well, if you give me your card,
I can pay for dry cleaning later.

480
00:29:10,720 --> 00:29:12,260
Do you have any idea
how much this outfit costs?

481
00:29:12,690 --> 00:29:14,790
Dry cleaning? Give me a break.
Forget it.

482
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:27,000
What happened?

483
00:29:29,570 --> 00:29:30,910
This is so annoying.

484
00:29:34,310 --> 00:29:35,310
Come on, let's go.

485
00:29:35,810 --> 00:29:37,650
Darn, it's completely ruined.

486
00:29:45,790 --> 00:29:46,920
Unbelievable.

487
00:30:20,490 --> 00:30:24,290
(A Trap Called Desire)

488
00:30:24,460 --> 00:30:27,300
Anyway, people who have nothing
sure love to stick together.

489
00:30:27,460 --> 00:30:29,770
I'm the next chairman
of the scholarship foundation.

490
00:30:29,900 --> 00:30:32,500
I think I found
what Hyun Jae received.

491
00:30:32,700 --> 00:30:37,170
So, right up until the end,
Hyun Jae died trying to help you.

492
00:30:37,270 --> 00:30:39,540
This was lying around.
Doesn't something feel off to you?

493
00:30:39,680 --> 00:30:41,950
If I dangle some bait right now,

494
00:30:42,110 --> 00:30:43,980
they'll walk right into the trap.

495
00:30:44,180 --> 00:30:46,650
Sir, please don't worry too much.

496
00:30:46,650 --> 00:30:48,250
I told you I'd protect you.

497
00:30:48,380 --> 00:30:50,490
What was your relationship
with my father?

498
00:30:50,650 --> 00:30:52,490
- My relationship with Seong Woo?
- Let go!

499
00:30:52,560 --> 00:30:55,760
Why the sudden interest
in that, Chief Cha?

500
00:30:56,790 --> 00:30:58,760
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
